Since angle of dip at a place is defined as the angle $\delta$, which is the direction of total intensity of earth's magnetic field $B$ makes with a horizontal line in magnetic meridian, At poles $B=B_V$ and $B_V=B \sin \delta $
\therefore \quad \sin \delta=1 \Rightarrow \delta=90^{\circ}
$$
At equator $B=B_H$ and $B_H=B \cos \delta $
\therefore \quad \cos \delta=1 \Rightarrow \delta=0^{\circ} \text{. }
